ThomasHarrisonNel...@gmail.com wrote:
>
> And also, it turns out Stormbringer is awesome.

It is one of the best weapons in the game, especially early on.
Be cautioned that in the end game many of the monsters are
immune to its level drain so by then it's just another rustproof
+7 weapon.  In other words it's still good enough to ascend
with.

Be cautioned.  All other weapons ask you if you want to
attack a peaceful monster or pet.  Stormy simply attacks.
That can be quite bad when you're still in the mines and the
monster it attacks is as strong as a priest.  When near certain
monsters switch to some other wielded weapon.

> I barely need my bow any more.

That's a trap.  Resist it fiercely.  For any character with missiles,
every type of melee is a backup.  Better melee does not replace
missile attacks it just means you're facing the monsters for less
time as they try to kill you.  A better weapon should NOT have
all that much impact on exploration and combat strategy.  It will
convert a few more monsters to popcorn level but on most levels
most monsters aren't popcorn even with artifacts better than
Stormy.

> Perhaps this is a FAQ, but are some alignments considered easier to
> ascend with than others?

Because of Excalibur, lawfuls are usually easiest.  But note my
comment above about melee weapons being a trap.  All artifacts
that can be gotten from altars are melee weapons.  The DevTeam
is devious indeed.

> I know there are some nice things about chaotic,

Get your diety angry with you and choatic is the hardest.  Don't
and more freedom allows chaotics extra options.  It's a bit of a
wash overall.

> and I guess it controls what kind of artifacts you can get,

Lawfuls can only get lawful or unaligned artifacts as gifts, neutrals
neutral and unaligned, chaotics chaotic and unaligned.  But
wishing remains an option and each alignment does have at
least one possible route to get 1 or 2 or its artifacts by any player.

> and what roles you can play. =A0Is chaotic truly the best, as it
> currently seems from my admittedly noobish point of view?

As with anything in Nethack "it depends" and "the opinion you
form early on will eventually be an opinion you no longer agree
with".  I think there's more variation by class than by alignment.


